## 10. Distance Estimation

![Distance estimation](/root/projects/ReplayAttack/iq_datasets/camera_flight_analysis/10_distance_estimation.png)

### Relative Distance Statistics

| Dataset | Min | Max | Range (Δ) | Far Peaks | Close Peaks |
|---------|-----|-----|-----------|-----------|-------------|
| Flight1 | 0.9843 | 1.0301 | **0.0458** | 10 | 9 |
| Flight2 | 0.9725 | 1.0329 | **0.0604** | 7 | 7 |
| Flight3 | 0.9769 | 1.0677 | **0.0909** | 49 | 47 |
| TakeOff | 0.9775 | 1.0410 | **0.0635** | 25 | 26 |

**Distance conclusions:**
- **Flight3 has the largest distance variation** (Δ=0.091) with 49 far peaks and 47 close peaks — confirms multiple fly-away-return cycles
- The relative distance oscillates around 1.0, showing clear approaching/departing patterns
- Flight1 shows the smallest variation — likely a shorter, less dramatic flight path
- The **number of peaks correlates with flight duration**, confirming consistent back-and-forth movement patterns

---

## 11. Landing Detection

![Landing detection](/root/projects/ReplayAttack/iq_datasets/camera_flight_analysis/11_landing_detection.png)

| Dataset | Landing Detected? | Evidence |
|---------|-------------------|----------|
| Flight1 | ❌ No | Power stabilized at end, but no other indicators |
| **Flight2** | ✅ **YES** | Power stabilized + power increased at end |
| Flight3 | ❌ No | Power increased at end (drone came back), but still dynamic |
| TakeOff | ❌ No | Power increased at end (return), but still moving |

> [!NOTE]
> **Flight2 shows the clearest landing signature** — power stabilization combined with increased power at the end (drone landed close). Flight3 and TakeOff show power increases at the end (drone returning) but the signal remains dynamic, suggesting the recording was stopped while the drone was still approaching. You mentioned some flights had landings — Flight2's data is consistent with a landing event.

